**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
.git/
.gitignore
README.md

# Never let developer secrets into the build context. All three Dockerfiles do
# `COPY . /src`, and the Web SDK publishes appsettings.*.json by default — without
# these, `docker compose up --build` bakes the local .env and Development config
# (API keys, DB passwords) into the published image.
#
# `*.env` as well as `.env*`, for the same reason .gitignore carries both: the two
# patterns do not overlap, and `prod.env` (or `odyssey.env`, the name Docker's own
# --env-file examples use) matches only the second.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example
**/appsettings.Development.json

# Local Claude state (settings.local.json can contain credentials)
.claude/
